# Example B1 with an alpha beam.
#
# The companion to proton.mac, and the energy is chosen so that the two are the same experiment
# with a different projectile: 840 MeV is 210 MeV per nucleon, and an alpha at 210 MeV/u has
# very nearly the same range in water as a 210 MeV proton (288 mm against 287 mm). The Bragg
# peak therefore lands in the same place inside Shape2, and the difference between the two runs
# is the projectile's charge and mass rather than where it stopped.
#
# Everything else is B1 exactly as it ships.
#
# As with proton.mac, this file on both sides compares against QBBC, which for an alpha adds
# hadElastic, alphaInelastic, ionElastic and ionInelastic that this port does not have.
# ref/b1hadron/alpha_emonly.mac is the like-for-like variant.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/gun/particle alpha
/gun/energy 840 MeV

/run/printProgress 2000
/run/beamOn 10000
